# Python Package Structure

## Layout per module

```
packages/module-{name}/
└── module_{name}/
    ├── api.py          # facade — sole cross-module entry
    ├── routes/         # HTTP adapter, when the module has HTTP
    ├── ports/
    ├── services/
    ├── adapters/
    └── schemas/
```

`module-ai` has `agents/` and no `routes/`.

## Naming

- Distribution: `module-metrics`. Import: `module_metrics`.
- Facade class: `{Domain}Module` (`MetricsModule`, `AiModule`).
- Service: `{Domain}Service`.

## Layering

```
routes/  →  api.py  →  services/  →  ports/  ←  adapters/
```

MCP tools call a facade method. They do not import `services/` or `agents/`.

## Shared libs

- `pulseboard-core` — ports and settings. No I/O.
- `pulseboard-models` — ORM only.
- `pulseboard-connectors` — I/O adapters.
